The conjecture concerns open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object. It states the documented rule is that an object nested inside another is not a candidate of its own. For Reply A '{"a": {"b": 1}, "c": }' the outer object is invalid, so the nested {"b": 1} should not be recovered; recover_json_object should raise RecordError. For Reply B '{"b": 1}' it should recover {"b": 1}. The observed check returns {"b": 1} for both, because the failed outer parse leaves the cursor before the nested object, which is then parsed as top-level. The conjecture would be wrong if recover_json_object raises RecordError for Reply A, or if the documented rule allows a nested object to be scored when its outer object is invalid.